One of the new items in slashem is a fishing pole. It has several uses,
including the most obvious one, which is to go fishing. When you fish,
you have a chance of catching cram rations. Basically, once you get a
fishing pole in slashem, and have found or can make a pool of water
(fountain+pickaxe: not exactly difficult to find) then you have,
effectively, infinite food.

Wihle some may consider this unbalancing, I don't think it's
necessarily a bug in need of fixing. What I do think needs fixing
though, is the fact that my vegan tourist can go fishing, catch stuff,
eat it and not break conduct, because cram rations count as vegan food.
I don't know of any vegans who would eat fish, and although I have
heard that some vegetarians do eat fish (?), I think fish meat should
violate nethack veggie conduct.

Therefore I propose that in future versions of slashem a new ; monster
is introduced: The fish.
When you go fishing, instead of a cram ration you reel in a live fish -
it appears on a square adjacent to the player. You then have to kill it
before you can eat it.

- Fish have only 1 hp (to avoid using them for easy weapons practise).
- Fish are always hostile, but have no attacks.
- Fish can be genocided, but not extincted (there's always more fish in
the sea=-)
- A fish corpse gives the same sort of nutrition as a lichen corpse,
but will spoil in time like (almost) any other corpse. This means that
you can still eat forever and for free with a fishing pole, but the
food will not be so portable. (unless you have a tinning kit.)
- Fish corpses have little or no value as sacrifices. (To avoid an
obvious abuse)
- Fish corpses break veggie and vegan conduct.
- Handling fish corpses make can your fingers slippy.

Anyone agree/ disagree with this? Thought I'd chuck the idea out here
for refinement before submitting it to the slashem team.

